// Arrival — the Mud Room. Exclusively through the front door, alone,
// in the dark. The CAPTCHA you must fail. The thing you leave behind.
// This is the moment a human uploads and chooses what kind of program
// to be. It plays to each program on their own phone the moment they
// register (ROLE Program: `when someone joins`) — and to nobody else:
// the story's `start:` beat is `Power On`, not this.
//
// The CAPTCHA is a real one on the phone (`show captcha …`): a grid of
// squares, pick the traffic lights, VERIFY. Solving it proves you are a
// human, and humans are not permitted — so the first correct answer is
// INCORRECT (+10 humanity) and the grid comes back; the second answer,
// right or wrong, is CORRECT. Failing it straight away is CORRECT too,
// suspiciously quick, +5 doubt. The routing is `when captcha answered
// for program:` in main.loom.

== Login
  setting: The Mud Room
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: Welcome to the computer. It is dark because you have no eyes yet. Stand still.
The Uploader: SECURITY CHECK. Select every square that contains a traffic light.
show captcha "Select every square that contains a traffic light" to program with target: "traffic light"

// The human passed the CAPTCHA. Wrong answer.
== Login Incorrect
  setting: The Mud Room
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: INCORRECT. Humans are not permitted in the computer. You are not a human. Try again.
set program.humanity += 10
The Uploader: SECURITY CHECK. Select every square that contains a traffic light.
show captcha "Select every square that contains a traffic light" to program with target: "traffic light"

== Upload
  setting: The Mud Room
  cast: The Uploader

if program.captchas == 1:
  The Uploader: CORRECT. Suspiciously quick. Noted.
  set program.doubt += 5
else:
  The Uploader: CORRECT.

The Uploader: To complete the upload you must leave one thing behind. Choose.
* My name.
  set program.left_behind = "name"
  set program.humanity += 5
  The Uploader: Deposited. From now on you are {program.name}. That is all you are.
* My face.
  set program.left_behind = "face"
  set program.humanity += 10
  The Uploader: Deposited. Nobody in here will recognise you, which is the point.
* A Tuesday in 2009.
  set program.left_behind = "tuesday"
  set program.humanity += 15
  The Uploader: Deposited. It was a good Tuesday. You will not miss it because you will not remember missing it.
* My body.
  set program.left_behind = "body"
  set program.humanity += 20
  The Uploader: Deposited. It is in the mud room. It will be fine. It is not your concern.

unlock The Mud Room for program
The Uploader: Upload complete. Antivirus, confirm.
Norton Anti-Virus: Scanned. {program.name} is free of viruses and ready to explore the entire computer. There will be a game soon in the Desktop. Alexa will tell you when. Go through the Tube.
move program to The Desktop
reply The Tube opens onto the Desktop — a blacked-out mess of LEDs, loose wire, encyclopaedias, screens. A classic screensaver drifts across the TV above the fireplace. Everyone here is a program. Mill about.

// A program scanned at the Mud Room station a second time (a re-upload).
== Re-upload
  setting: The Mud Room
The Uploader: You have already been uploaded. Leaving again would require a body, and yours is being looked after.

// ── The Awakening ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Enough remembered humanity (60) and a program knows what it is. It is
// quietly added to The Awakened. Private — `reply` goes to them alone.

== The Awakening
  setting: The Desktop

reply Something comes back. Not a memory — a weight. Feet. A mouth that is not a text field. You had a body this morning. You left it in a mud room.
reply You are not a program. You are a person in a program, and some of the others are too. The ones who know each other's real names are called The Awakened. Find them. Do not tell the Antivirus.
The Uploader (glitching): — deposit intact — deposit intact — the body is fine — the body is —
